  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR satellite session at the 15th Internation Health Economics Association (IHEA) World Congress on Health Economics</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Raise the profile of NIHR in the global health research funding landscape
2. Bring together researchers and thought-leaders to inform the development of the NIHR Global Health Research programme&#x2019;s future activities in health economics
3. Provide support to the participation of low-and-middle-income country (LMIC) based speakers in the Symposium</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To inform the development of a dedicated NIHR-led health economics programme and activities, NIHR is undertaking outreach and consultation activities to establish areas where there is an unmet need or skill shortage and areas which are under-funded or under-researched. The 15th International Health Economics Association (IHEA) World Congress on Health Economics presented a unique opportunity for NIHR to engage in an international event and consult stakeholders on key methodologies, impactful policy research and  capacity strenghtening  through the organisation of a dedicated satellite session.</narrative>
  </description>
